  "name": "savanna-acacia",
  "notes": "Flat-topped umbrella crown on a bare trunk. The silhouette is the whole species, so crown.shape and the low crown.height_frac matter more here than anything else.\nThe leafy layer is a thin disc, not a ball, so a clump sized like an oak's spans the whole thickness of it and reads as a plate. This species therefore runs a smaller clump_radius_m and far more of them, and walks foliage.compensate back to 0.20 where the rest of the library sits at 0.60 -- compensation grows the survivors of the separation pass, which is exactly the few-big-plates picture this crown must avoid. crown.points and growth.kill_m come with it: more, smaller clumps need more twigs to hang on, and at 1300 points this crown was seeded coarser than the oak's despite being the same width.",
